    "text": {
     "en": "(additional, not in the textbook) A habitat is the natural home of a plant or animal.\nAnimals have special body parts that help them live in their habitat, called adaptations.\nBirds have feathers and wings to fly. Fish have fins to swim.\nSome animals match their surroundings, called camouflage, so enemies cannot see them."
